<SpecLayout title="Playtest feedback">
  <h1>November 1 playtest fixes</h1>
  <p>These requirements refine the existing shop, free-field, trap and feedback contracts.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Shop body headers MUST span the body card. Meseta MUST appear at its bottom right and refresh after transactions. The item shop MUST show only the meseta footer, without a directions footer. Its header MUST have rounded upper corners and a visible border. Item-shop rows MUST show a fixed marker slot ([E], ✕, or blank), then the icon, spacing, and item text. The modal border MUST be 3px; the Meseta: footer MUST sit directly against the bottom border without extra blue padding. Footer corners MUST follow the modal’s inner radius. Vertical list scrollbars MUST remain visible even on short lists, with an 8px gap on their left. Description layout remains a separate task.</li>
    <li>Miss feedback MUST be smaller than damage numbers and red. Awarded EXP MUST appear once in purple, using the actual reward (for example +75 exp).</li>
    <li>Enemy defeat MUST have an audible cue, preserving authored death-animation sounds where available.</li>
    <li>A newly dropped room key MUST play an arrival cue; restoring an existing key MUST NOT replay that cue.</li>
    <li>A recovery cube MUST play SE_SYS_WINCLOSE (common_186.wav) only when it actually heals and MUST become dark grey after use. Full-HP contact MUST NOT consume it.</li>
    <li>Room-change waypoints MUST NOT cast shadows. Flyer reticles MUST follow the animated visual body.</li>
    <li>Turret hurtboxes MUST extend to the visible body and allow melee contact without standing inside it; firing and destruction behavior are unchanged.</li>
    <li>Entering a section start without an explicit room-entry edge MUST use that section's authored entry direction. Explicit backtracking and room-to-room entry MUST retain their destination edge. Valley E and B starts MUST enter from south, with north remaining negative Z as in the stage editor.</li>
    <li>Underground static mirrored surfaces MUST use the existing offline native-material bake. Unsupported animated surfaces MUST retain their shader path. Runtime MUST NOT bake textures.</li>
  <li>The Valley entry diagnostic MUST load the production Valley B room in an isolated save namespace, label the physical north/south portals, and verify that the initial player marker is nearest the south portal on the minimap. For s01b_sa1, south MUST be portal_1769178737883_7bppcx8w1 (Valley E transition); north MUST be portal_1769178748150_zpfcscb89 (planked slope into Valley B). Portal identity, not the sign of Z, defines this thematic entry. Physical gate orientation and trigger positions MUST stay unchanged. Retained fields MUST use the corrected mapping.</li>
    <li>Dairon Market MUST animate the authored background NPC atlas at six frames per second and drift soft cloud shadows across ground surfaces. These visuals MUST retain depth occlusion and MUST NOT add collision or change navigation. Cloud appearance requires a visual playtest.</li>
    <li>Elemental and bomb traps MUST show a short blast at their gameplay origin, with the same world-space radius as their damage query. Unused expired traps MUST NOT show a blast. Burn flames MUST follow players and enemies while active and disappear immediately on cure, expiry or defeat, including when other statuses remain.</li>
    <li>Boxes and breakable walls MUST share a short destruction burst distributed across the destroyed model bounds. Shards MUST be smaller than the object and disappear within 0.7 seconds. Repeated destruction and restored destroyed state MUST NOT replay effects or duplicate loot. Collision removal, wall hit counts and persistent state MUST remain unchanged.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Validation includes seeded entry-selection tests and a runtime feedback/transition probe. Visual and audio acceptance remains subject to playtesting.</p>
</SpecLayout>
